      {"h2": "A surprising detail from history",
       "paras": ["The twelve animals were not always exactly the ones we know. Bamboo slips from a Qin tomb at Shuihudi, sealed in 217 BCE, record an animal cycle in which a deer stands where the Horse is now, and a horse stands where the Goat is now. By the time of Wang Chong's <em>Lunheng</em> in the first century CE, the familiar list had settled. More on this in <a href=\"why-12-animals-chinese-zodiac\">Why Are There 12 Animals?</a>"]},
